From 5ca0c078b27c73946cf788317bac089395ee4096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deck <jenergy@tiscali.it>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:46:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Gate Sprint features via ADD_JZINTV_MENU + build.sh
 SPRINT_FEATURES

Decouple the Sprint in-game popup menu from the build-identity macro and
route optional Sprint features through build.sh.

Sources: every menu block (jzintv.h/.c, event.c, event_sdl.c, event_plat.h,
gfx_sdl2.c) is now wrapped in an outer #ifdef JZINTV_SPRINT and an inner
#ifdef ADD_JZINTV_MENU, so the menu compiles only inside a Sprint build AND
when the menu feature is enabled.

Build:
  * src/Makefile.sprint keeps DEF_FLAGS = -DJZINTV_SPRINT (intrinsic, always
    on) and adds an empty FEATURES ?= appended to CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS.
  * build.sh has a new SPRINT_FEATURES knob (default -DADD_JZINTV_MENU),
    handed to make as FEATURES=..., documented in its header. Its behaviour
    is unchanged by default; 'SPRINT_FEATURES="" ./build.sh sprint' builds a
    Sprint without the menu.
  * build.sh now echoes the parameters in effect (target + env knobs) before
    building, so they are reported even when a target aborts early (e.g. the
    ARM cross-compiler is missing).

Add ReleaseNotes_20260816.txt describing the change (behaviour-neutral).
